      "created_at": "2026-01-09T19:57:23.612Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Hi All,</p>\n<p>This feels like a BUG if not please let me know</p>\n<p>Here are the steps:</p>\n<p>A Sales Order is Created and Pick List is Created for it.</p>\n<p>Sales Order is Canceled which cancels the Pick List for it.</p>\n<p>Sales Order is Amended.</p>\n<p>Cannot create a Pick List for Amended Sales Order. In Sales Order Item picked_qty=2</p>\n<p>Delete the canceled Pick List for the original Sales Order still same issue.</p>\n<p>** To TEST I forced the picked_qty=0 in original &amp; amended Sales Order Items. Same Issue.</p>\n<p>if SO is cancelled and PL is canceled why picked_qty &gt;0</p>\n<p>After I force the picked_qty=0 (using a script) Why I still get the same issue. Where else the system keeps track of picked_qty? I looked at Stock Reservation Entry and it is empty.</p>\n<p>Help please</p>\n<p>Thanks</p>",
